"""Run one round participant through a provider API and keep the evidence.

Usage:
    python tools/run_api_participant.py PROVIDER MODEL EVIDENCE_PREFIX
        [--tag round/01-deliberation/v1]
        [--history-record RECORD_PATH [--history-tag round/00-initial/v1]]
        [--max-output-tokens N] [--max-input-tokens N] [--keys-file PATH]

PROVIDER is gemini (Google Gemini API, generateContent) or xai (xAI chat completions).

Keys come from a private file of KEY=value lines (default: .private/api-keys.env
next to the repository folder). A key is sent only in a request header. It is
never written to evidence, printed, or put in a URL.

Evidence files, each created exclusively, so nothing is ever overwritten:
    PREFIX.preflight.json  model metadata, the request body, history provenance,
                           and an input token count from the provider's counting
                           endpoint (no generation), written before anything is sent
    PREFIX.attempt.json    the attempt record, written BEFORE the request
    PREFIX.stream.sse      every line of the streamed response, as raw bytes, before decoding
    PREFIX.result.json     completed: answer, thought summary or reasoning if returned,
                           finish reason, usage, returned model and response IDs, response headers
    PREFIX.failure.json    an error after the attempt started: error, HTTP status and body, partial output

With --history-record, the participant's earlier exchange is sent first: the
earlier round's participant text (from --history-tag), then the earlier answer,
taken from the committed record body. Each model's own roles are used (Gemini:
user/model; xAI: user/assistant).

No sampling settings are overridden: temperature and similar settings are the
provider's defaults, recorded as unknown unless returned. No tools, search, or
system instruction are sent. That does not prove the provider adds nothing.

One run is one attempt. The script never retries. If any evidence file already
exists, it refuses to start.
"""
